LS.add({"bc63b4f664":{"t":"S20 conscience 良心","b":1,"k":"unit","h":"<nav class=\"cr\" style=\"--c:#c0841a\"><a href=\"index.html\">燈臺 <i lang=\"en\">The Lampstand</i></a> <span class=\"sep\">›</span> <a class=\"fl0\" href=\"#ic52d1cf364\">1 原文研究 Original Languages</a> <span class=\"sep\">›</span> <a class=\"fl1\" href=\"#ie883cc6886\">1 詞彙 Vocabulary</a> <span class=\"sep\">›</span> <a class=\"fl2\" href=\"#i52badd311e\">Studies 研究</a></nav><h1 class=\"fl3\" id=\"s20--良心-conscience\">S20 · <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> conscience</h1><details class=\"toc\"><summary>目錄 <i lang=\"en\">Contents</i></summary><ol><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\">1. At a glance 一覽</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#2-root-and-family-%E5%AD%97%E6%A0%B9%E8%88%87%E5%AD%97%E6%97%8F\">2. Root and family 字根與字族</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#3-counts-and-significance-%E6%95%B8%E6%93%9A%E8%88%87%E6%84%8F%E7%BE%A9\">3. Counts and significance 數據與意義</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#1-totals-%E7%B8%BD%E6%95%B8\">1. Totals 總數</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#2-by-book-%E6%8C%89%E6%9B%B8%E5%8D%B7\">2. By book 按書卷</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#3-by-section-%E6%8C%89%E5%88%86%E6%AE%B5\">3. By section 按分段</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#4-by-grammatical-form-%E6%8C%89%E8%A9%9E%E5%BD%A2\">4. By grammatical form 按詞形</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#5-by-translation-%E6%8C%89%E8%AD%AF%E6%9C%AC\">5. By translation 按譯本</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#6-first-and-last-use-rank-hapax-%E9%A6%96%E6%AC%A1%E8%88%87%E6%9C%AB%E6%AC%A1%E6%8E%92%E5%90%8D%E7%BD%95%E7%94%A8\">6. First and last use; rank; hapax 首次與末次、排名、罕用</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#7-spread-%E5%88%86%E4%BD%88\">7. Spread 分佈</a></li><li class=\"l3\"><a href=\"#8-significance-%E6%84%8F%E7%BE%A9\">8. Significance 意義</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#4-%E5%92%8C%E5%90%88%E6%9C%AC-renderings-%E5%92%8C%E5%90%88%E6%9C%AC%E7%9A%84%E8%AD%AF%E6%B3%95-every-rendering-every-verse\">4. 和合本 renderings 和合本的譯法 (every rendering, every verse)</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#5-shades-of-meaning-%E6%84%8F%E7%BE%A9%E5%B1%A4%E6%AC%A1\">5. Shades of meaning 意義層次</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#6-the-lxx-bridge-%E4%B8%83%E5%8D%81%E5%A3%AB%E8%AD%AF%E6%9C%AC%E7%9A%84%E6%A9%8B%E6%A8%91\">6. The LXX bridge 七十士譯本的橋樑</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#7-companions-and-cross-references-%E5%90%8C%E4%BC%B4%E5%AD%97%E8%88%87%E4%BA%92%E5%8F%83\">7. Companions and cross-references 同伴字與互參</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#8-in-the-new-testament-%E6%96%B0%E7%B4%84%E7%9A%84%E7%94%A8%E6%B3%95\">8. In the New Testament 新約的用法</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#9-culture-and-background-%E6%96%87%E5%8C%96%E8%83%8C%E6%99%AF\">9. Culture and background 文化背景</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#10-theology-%E7%A5%9E%E5%AD%B8\">10. Theology 神學</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#12-for-practice-%E6%87%89%E7%94%A8\">11. For practice 應用</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#13-evaluation-%E8%A9%95%E4%BC%B0\">12. Evaluation 評估</a></li><li class=\"l2\"><a href=\"#14-sources-and-to-check-%E8%B3%87%E6%96%99%E8%88%87%E5%BE%85%E6%9F%A5\">13. Sources 資料</a></li></ol></details>\n<p><span class=\"off\">Man <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">人論</span></span> · <span class=\"off\">Salvation <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">救恩論</span></span><span class=\"off\"></span></p>\n<h2 id=\"1-at-a-glance-一覽\">1. At a glance <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">一覽</span></h2>\n<p><strong>Hebrew:</strong> <big><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span></big> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></p>\n<p><strong>Greek:</strong> <big><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span></big> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span> · <big><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span></big> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span> · <big><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span></big> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A New Testament word; the Old Testament says 'heart'.</strong> <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> stands 30 times in 29 verses, from \"Brethren, I have lived before God in all good conscience until this day\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>, ASV) to \"the interrogation of a good conscience toward God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>, ASV). The Hebrew Bible has no word for it, and the KJV says 'conscience' only in the NT (32 times in 30 verses; section 8 gives the differences). Where we say 'conscience' the Hebrew says 'heart': \"that David's heart smote him\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>, ASV) — <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">וַ יַּ֥ךְ לֵב־ דָּוִ֖ד אֹתֹ֑ו</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>, BHSA), in the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本 「隨後大衛心中自責」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>. BDB gives <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span> and <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵבָב</span> each a sense '5. specific reference to conscience', for this verse and for \"My heart shall not reproach me so long as I live\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li><strong>Knowing with oneself.</strong> The word is <span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> 'with' + the stem of <span lang=\"grc\">οἶδα</span> 'know': Strong's, 'from a prolonged form of <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span>' (<span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> and <span lang=\"grc\">εἴδω</span>); Abbott-Smith derives it from <span lang=\"grc\">συνεῖδον</span>. LSJ's senses climb from 'knowledge shared with another' and 'knowledge' to '4 consciousness, awareness' and '5 consciousness of right or wrong doing, conscience', and it adds: 'Senses 4 and 5 sometimes run one into the other'. A person is both the one who acts and the one who knows what he did — a witness inside. The verb shows both steps: Ananias kept back part of the price, \"his wife also being privy to it\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span>, ASV) (knowledge shared with another), and Paul says <em><span lang=\"grc\">οὐδὲν γὰρ ἐμαυτῷ σύνοιδα</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, OpenGNT), \"For I know nothing against myself; yet am I not hereby justified\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li><strong>The witness and the judge.</strong> In Paul the conscience 'bears witness' — with <span lang=\"grc\">συμμαρτυρέω</span> in 2 verses (chance alone 0.0): \"their conscience bearing witness therewith\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>, ASV) and \"my conscience bearing witness with me in the Holy Spirit\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>, ASV) — and gives \"the testimony of our conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.1.12\">2 Cor 1:12</span>, ASV). ISBE (1915, CONSCIENCE) names its two sides: the 'Sequent Conscience—that is to say, it follows action', which 'has often been compared to a court of law, in which there are culprit, judge, witnesses and jury; but these are all in the subject's own breast, and are in fact himself'; and 'the Antecedent Conscience, which designates a function of this faculty preceding moral decision or action'. But the inner court is not the last one: \"but he that judgeth me is the Lord\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, ASV); \"if our heart condemn us, God is greater than our heart, and knoweth all things\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li><strong>Good or evil, strong or weak.</strong> The words beside it tell its states (Abbott-Smith lists them): good, <span lang=\"grc\">ἀγαθή</span> (5 verses (chance alone 0.3): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">1 Pet 3:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">21</span>); pure, <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρά</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">1 Tim 3:9</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>); honourable, <span lang=\"grc\">καλή</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span>); <em><span lang=\"grc\">ἀπρόσκοπον συνείδησιν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, OpenGNT), \"a conscience void of offence toward God and men always\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, ASV). On the other side: weak (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.10\">10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">12</span>), defiled (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>), evil, <em><span lang=\"grc\">ἀπὸ συνειδήσεως πονηρᾶς</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>, OpenGNT), and branded, <em><span lang=\"grc\">κεκαυστηριασμένων τὴν ἰδίαν συνείδησιν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>, OpenGNT), \"branded in their own conscience as with a hot iron\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li><strong>Where it stands (log-likelihood):</strong> none in the Gospels (fewer than their size predicts, G² 38) and none in Revelation; Paul's letters 20, Hebrews and the General letters 8, Acts 2 (both in Paul's own speeches). By book: 1 Corinthians has the most (8, G² 16: the weak conscience and the meat offered to idols, chapters 8 and 10), then Hebrews (5, G² 8), 1 Timothy (4, G² 13, the highest rate: 25.1 per 10,000 words) and 1 Peter (3, G² 8).</li>\n<li><strong>Hebrews: the worshipper's conscience.</strong> All five uses in Hebrews stand in 9:9–10:22 and 13:18, and three of them beside <span lang=\"grc\">λατρεύω</span> 'serve, worship' (4 verses (chance alone 0.1); the fourth verse is <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>). The old gifts and sacrifices are those \"that cannot, as touching the conscience, make the worshipper perfect\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>, ASV); but \"how much more shall the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without blemish unto God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, ASV) The old worshippers kept <em><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησιν ἁμαρτιῶν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span>, OpenGNT), a 'consciousness of sins'; the new draw near \"having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li><strong>The Septuagint's one use.</strong> In the LXX used here (the 39 books only) <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> stands once: <em><span lang=\"grc\">και γε εν συνειδήσει σου βασιλέα μη καταράση</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, ABP) for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">גַּ֣ם בְּ מַדָּֽעֲךָ֗ מֶ֚לֶךְ אַל־ תְּקַלֵּ֔ל</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, BHSA), \"Revile not the king, no, not in thy thought\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, ASV) (<span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本 「也不可心懷此念」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>). The verb <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> turns Job's 'my heart shall not reproach me' into conscience language: <em><span lang=\"grc\">ου γαρ σύνοιδα εμαυτώ άτοπα πράξας</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>, ABP) ('for I am not conscious of having done anything amiss', a plain rendering) — the words of <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, <span lang=\"grc\">ἐμαυτῷ σύνοιδα</span>.</li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本: 良心, 天良, 是非之心</span>.</strong> The <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> says <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> for <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> 26 times, <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">天良</span> twice (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>), <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span> once, <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「他們是非之心同作見證」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>, and in <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span> <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span> with a note, <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「洗淨你們的心〔原文作良心〕」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>. It also writes <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> twice where the original has no such word: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「良心既然喪盡」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eph.4.19\">Eph 4:19</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span> for <span lang=\"grc\">ἀπηλγηκότες</span>, \"who being past feeling\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eph.4.19\">Eph 4:19</span>, ASV), and Abigail's words to David, <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「那時我主必不至心裏不安，覺得良心有虧」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.25.30-31\">1 Sam 25:30-31</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span> for \"nor offence of heart unto my lord\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.25.30-31\">1 Sam 25:30-31</span>, ASV) (BDB under <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span>: 'offence of conscience').</li>\n<li><strong>First and last.</strong> The first: \"Brethren, I have lived before God in all good conscience until this day\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>, ASV) — and at once \"And the high priest Ananias commanded them that stood by him to smite him on the mouth\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.2\">Acts 23:2</span>, ASV). The last: \"which also after a true likeness doth now save you, even baptism, not the putting away of the filth of the flesh, but the interrogation of a good conscience toward God, through the resurrection of Jesus Christ\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>, ASV) (KJV \"the answer of a good conscience toward God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>, KJV)).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">看圖</span> See it</strong> — the counts by book and by section are the two charts of section 3; the renderings with their counts are sections 3.7 and 4:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bible circles <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聖經圓圖</span>: <span class=\"off\">Hebrews 9, the conscience cleansed</span> · <span class=\"off\">1 Corinthians 8, the weak conscience</span> · <span class=\"off\">1 Timothy 1, a good conscience</span> · <span class=\"off\">Romans 2, the law on the heart</span> · <span class=\"off\">1 Samuel 24, David's heart smote him</span> · the app itself: <span class=\"off\">the circles (file)</span></li>\n<li>People (the circles' people, four languages): <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅</span> Paul <span lang=\"grc\">Παῦλος</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">24:16</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">亞拿尼亞</span> Ananias <span lang=\"grc\">Ἁνανίας</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.2\">Acts 23:2</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">腓力斯</span> Felix <span lang=\"grc\">Φῆλιξ</span></span> (Acts 24) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">大衛</span> David <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דָּוִד</span> <span lang=\"grc\">Δαυίδ</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">掃羅</span> Saul <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">שָׁאוּל</span> <span lang=\"grc\">Σαούλ</span></span> · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">亞比米勒</span> Abimelech <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֲבִימֶלֶךְ</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">約伯</span> Job <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אִיּוֹב</span> <span lang=\"grc\">Ἰώβ</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">亞拿尼亞</span> Ananias <span lang=\"grc\">Ἁνανίας</span></span> and <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">撒非喇</span> Sapphira <span lang=\"grc\">Σαπφείρη</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">提摩太</span> Timothy <span lang=\"grc\">Τιμόθεος</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">提多</span> Titus <span lang=\"grc\">Τίτος</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>)</li>\n<li>Places: <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">基拉耳</span> Gerar <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">גְּרָר</span></span> <span class=\"off\">🗺 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">地圖</span> map</span> (Gen 20) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">耶路撒冷</span> Jerusalem <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יְרוּשָׁלַ</span>͏<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">ִם</span> <span lang=\"grc\">Ἰερουσαλήμ</span></span> <span class=\"off\">🗺 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">地圖</span> map</span> (Acts 23) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">該撒利亞</span> Caesarea <span lang=\"grc\">Καισάρεια</span></span> <span class=\"off\">🗺 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">地圖</span> map</span> (Acts 24) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">哥林多</span> Corinth <span lang=\"grc\">Κόρινθος</span></span> <span class=\"off\">🗺 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">地圖</span> map</span> (1 Cor 8; 10) · <span class=\"off\">the Holy Land in 3D <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聖地立體地圖</span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><div class=\"zh\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">何況基督藉着永遠的靈，將自己無瑕無疵獻給神，他的血豈不更能洗淨你們的心〔原文作良心〕，除去你們的死行，使你們事奉那永生神嗎？（<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">希伯來書 9:14</span>）</span></div><div class=\"en\">how much more shall the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without blemish unto God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God? (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Hebrews 9:14</span>, ASV)</div></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><div class=\"zh\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">並我們心中天良的虧欠已經灑去，身體用清水洗淨了，就當存着誠心和充足的信心來到神面前；（<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">希伯來書 10:22</span>）</span></div><div class=\"en\">let us draw near with a true heart in fulness of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience: and having our body washed with pure water, (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Hebrews 10:22</span>, ASV)</div></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><div class=\"zh\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">我因此自己勉勵，對神對人，常存無虧的良心。（<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">使徒行傳 24:16</span>）</span></div><div class=\"en\">Herein I also exercise myself to have a conscience void of offence toward God and men always. (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, ASV)</div></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><div class=\"zh\"><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">但命令的總歸就是愛；這愛是從清潔的心和無虧的良心，無偽的信心生出來的。（<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">提摩太前書 1:5</span>）</span></div><div class=\"en\">But the end of the charge is love out of a pure heart and a good conscience and faith unfeigned: (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Timothy 1:5</span>, ASV)</div></blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"2-root-and-family-字根與字族\">2. Root and family <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">字根與字族</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><strong>Root <big><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span></big> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span></strong> — a primitive root</p>\n<p><strong>Stems <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">字幹</span> (binyanim) of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span></strong> — 939 of the 942 words tagged H3045 are verb forms (BHSA; participles and infinitives included), in the grammar sheets' order:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stem <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">字幹</span></th><th>Meaning <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">意思</span></th><th>Times</th><th>Share</th><th>First use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Qal (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>simple active <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">簡單主動</span></td><td>814</td><td>87%</td></tr><tr><td>Niphal (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>simple passive or reflexive <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">簡單被動或反身</span></td><td>41</td><td>4%</td></tr><tr><td>Piel (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>intensive active <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">加強主動</span></td><td>1</td><td>&lt;1%</td></tr><tr><td>Pual (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>intensive passive <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">加強被動</span></td><td>6</td><td>&lt;1%</td></tr><tr><td>Hiphil (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>causative active <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使役主動</span></td><td>71</td><td>8%</td></tr><tr><td>Hophal (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>causative passive <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使役被動</span></td><td>3</td><td>&lt;1%</td></tr><tr><td>Hithpael (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</td><td>intensive reflexive <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">加強反身</span></td><td>2</td><td>&lt;1%</td></tr><tr><td>Polal (Poal)</td><td>intensive passive, as Pual <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">加強被動（如</span> Pual<span lang=\"zh-Hant\">）</span></td><td>1</td><td>&lt;1%</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.21.2\">1 Sam 21:2</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>All stems</strong></td><td></td><td><strong>939</strong></td><td>100%</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Built on it (Strong's data)</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Times</th><th>In this study</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דַּעַת</span> <em>daʻath</em> <span class=\"off\">H1847</span></td><td>knowledge</td><td>95</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדּוּעַ</span> <em>maddûwaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4069</span></td><td>why · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מָה</span> *mâh</em> <span class=\"off\">H4100</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>72</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יְהוֹיָדָע</span> <em>Yᵉhôwyâdâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3077</span></td><td>Jehoiada · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יְהֹוָה</span> *Yᵉhôvâh</em> <span class=\"off\">H3068</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>51</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יְדַעְיָה</span> <em>Yᵉdaʻyâh</em> <span class=\"off\">H3048</span></td><td>Jedaiah · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> *yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָהּ</span> <em>Yâhh</em> <span class=\"off\">H3050</span>*</td><td>11</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יִדְּעֹנִי</span> <em>yiddᵉʻônîy</em> <span class=\"off\">H3049</span></td><td>soothsayer</td><td>11</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יְדִיעֲאֵל</span> <em>Yᵉdîyʻăʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H3043</span></td><td>Jediael · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> *yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֵל</span> <em>ʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H410</span>*</td><td>6</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></td><td>knowledge</td><td>6</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דֵּעַ</span> <em>dêaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H1843</span></td><td>knowledge</td><td>5</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֶלְיָדָע</span> <em>ʼElyâdâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H450</span></td><td>Eliada · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֵל</span> *ʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H410</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דְּעוּאֵל</span> <em>Dᵉʻûwʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H1845</span></td><td>Deuel · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> *yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֵל</span> <em>ʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H410</span>*</td><td>4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יַדּוּעַ</span> <em>Yaddûwaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3037</span></td><td>Jaddua</td><td>3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">שְׁמִידָע</span> <em>Shᵉmîydâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H8061</span></td><td>Shemida · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">שֵׁם</span> *shêm</em> <span class=\"off\">H8034</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֲבִידָע</span> <em>ʼĂbîydâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H28</span></td><td>Abida · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אָב</span> *ʼâb</em> <span class=\"off\">H1</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֶלְדָּעָה</span> <em>ʼEldâʻâh</em> <span class=\"off\">H420</span></td><td>Eldaah · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">אֵל</span> *ʼêl</em> <span class=\"off\">H410</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדָע</span> <em>Yâdâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3047</span></td><td>Jada</td><td>2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בְּעֶלְיָדָע</span> <em>Bᵉʻelyâdâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H1182</span></td><td>Beeliada · <em>compound of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בַּעַל</span> *Baʻal</em> <span class=\"off\">H1168</span> + <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> <em>yâdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H3045</span>*</td><td>1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מוֹדַע</span> <em>môwdaʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4129</span></td><td>kinsman</td><td>1</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מוֹדַעַת</span> <em>môwdaʻath</em> <span class=\"off\">H4130</span></td><td>kinsman</td><td>1</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>The whole family (Strong's data, every level):</em> 21 words — the 18 above and 3 built on them.</p>\n<p><strong>Compounds in this study (Strong's data):</strong> <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span> = <span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> <em>sýn</em> <span class=\"off\">G4862</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">εἴδω</span> <em>eídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G1492</span>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> (G4893): Strong's, 'from a prolonged form of <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span>' (G4894), which is 'from <span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> G4862 and <span lang=\"grc\">εἴδω</span> G1492'; Abbott-Smith, '(&lt; <span lang=\"grc\">συνεῖδον</span>)'. The verb is in the NT four times, in two tenses: the perfect <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> 'I know with', which OpenGNT numbers G6083 — <em><span lang=\"grc\">συνειδυίης καὶ τῆς γυναικός</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span>, OpenGNT) ('his wife also knowing it with him') and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span> — and the aorist, G4894, \"And when he had considered the thing\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.12.12\">Acts 12:12</span>, ASV) (Peter, freed from prison) and \"they became aware of it\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.14.6\">Acts 14:6</span>, ASV). The KJV's own Strong's numbers put all four under G4894 ('consider, know, be privy, be ware of'). The root verb <span lang=\"grc\">οἶδα</span> / <span lang=\"grc\">εἴδω</span> 'know, see' stands 658 times.</li>\n<li>The Greek ladder (LSJ): 'knowledge shared with another' (2nd century AD), 'communication, information', '3 knowledge' (5th century BC), '4 consciousness, awareness … inner consciousness, <span lang=\"grc\">ἐν σ. σου βασιλέα μὴ καταράσῃ</span> [LXX+NT]' — the Septuagint's <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span> — and '5 consciousness of right or wrong doing, conscience', with the line <span lang=\"grc\">βροτοῖς ἅπασιν ἡ σ. θεός</span> ('to all mortals conscience is a god', which LSJ dates to the 4th century BC; its author is not named in the local entry). Abbott-Smith: '1. consciousness: c. gen. obj., <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">He 10:2</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">I Pe 2:19</span>. 2. In ethical sense, innate discernment, self-judging consciousness, conscience (Stoics and late writers)'. The word was at home in Greek moral talk before Paul; the NT sets it 'before God' (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>), 'in the Holy Spirit' (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>), 'toward God' (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>).</li>\n<li>The Hebrew 'knowing' word: <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> (H4093), from <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> 'know' (942 times). BDB: 'knowledge, thought (late)', six times — Solomon's request for 'wisdom and knowledge' (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10-12\">2 Chr 1:10–12</span>), the young men of Daniel 1 (1:4, 17), and '2. place of knowledge, mind, (in our idiom also) thought' in <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בְּ מַדָּֽעֲךָ֗</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, BHSA) 'in thy thought' (BHSA: the noun with the suffix 'your'). The Greek verb <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> stands for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span> itself in the law of the witness: \"he being a witness, whether he hath seen or known\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span>, ASV) — <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">וְ ה֣וּא עֵ֔ד אֹ֥ו רָאָ֖ה אֹ֣ו יָדָ֑ע</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span>, BHSA) — <em><span lang=\"grc\">και ούτος μάρτυς η εώρακεν η συνοίδεν</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span>, ABP). In both languages the word begins with knowing.</li>\n<li>The heart for the conscience (BDB sense 5 of each): <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span> (H3820, 593 times) — <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">וַ יַּ֥ךְ לֵב־ דָּוִ֖ד אֹתֹ֑ו</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>, BHSA) 'and David's heart smote him' (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">וַיַּךְ</span> is the Hiphil wayyiqtol of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">נָכָה</span> 'strike', the III-he ending dropped; <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב־</span> stands in construct before <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דָּוִד</span>: grammar pages 2 and 4), again after the census, \"And David's heart smote him after that he had numbered the people\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>, ASV), and Abigail's <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מִכְשׁוֹל לֵב</span>, \"offence of heart\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.25.30-31\">1 Sam 25:30-31</span>, ASV) (BDB: 'offence of conscience'). <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵבָב</span> (H3824, 252 times) — <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֹֽא־ יֶחֱרַ֥ף לְ֝בָבִ֗י מִ יָּמָֽי</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>, BHSA) 'my heart shall not reproach me so long as I live' (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יֶחֱרַף</span>, Qal imperfect of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">חָרַף</span>, with a hateph vowel under the guttural; <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לְבָבִי</span>, 'my heart'). 'Integrity of heart' — <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בְּ תָם־ לְבָבִ֛י</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>, BHSA) — stands with <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵבָב</span> in 5 verses (chance alone 0.2): Abimelech, \"in the integrity of my heart and the innocency of my hands have I done this\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>, ASV), God's answer, \"Yea, I know that in the integrity of thy heart thou hast done this\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.6\">Gen 20:6</span>, ASV), Solomon (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Kgs.9.4\">1 Kgs 9:4</span>) and David (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Ps.78.72\">Ps 78:72</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Ps.101.2\">101:2</span>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"3-counts-and-significance-數據與意義\">3. Counts and significance <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">數據與意義</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><em>Sources: OT = BHSA (ETCBC words, prefixes count as words); NT = OpenGNT 3.3; KJV and ASV = eBible texts with Strong's tags; <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> = the word-by-word alignments (OpenHebrewBible, OpenGNT). Tests: log-likelihood G² with 1 degree of freedom.</em></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-totals-總數\">1. Totals <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">總數</span></h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lemma</th><th>Testament</th><th>Words</th><th>Verses</th><th>Forms</th><th>Commonest forms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span></td><td>NT</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>6</td><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησιν</span> 16, <span lang=\"grc\">συνειδήσεως</span> 6, <span lang=\"grc\">συνειδήσει</span> 3</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> family</strong></td><td>NT</td><td><strong>30</strong></td><td><strong>29</strong></td><td>6</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span></td><td>NT</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνειδυίης</span> 1, <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></td><td>NT</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td><span lang=\"grc\">Συνιδών</span> 1, <span lang=\"grc\">συνιδόντες</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span> family</strong></td><td>NT</td><td><strong>4</strong></td><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>4</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></td><td>OT</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּ֔ע</span> 2, <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע֙</span> 1, <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַּדָּ֖ע</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> family</strong></td><td>OT</td><td><strong>6</strong></td><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>5</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Whole Bible:</strong> 6 Hebrew words + 34 Greek words = 40 (the two languages are counted in their own texts; the Septuagint is not added).</p>\n<p><strong>Lexeme check (Strong's tag against the BHSA lexeme):</strong> every word counted carries the same BHSA lexeme as its Strong's number.</p>\n<h3 id=\"2-by-book-按書卷\">2. By book <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">按書卷</span></h3>\n<p><img class=\"emb\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"charts/S20 conscience - books.svg\" src=\"pages/ef0b4d5120.svg\"></p>\n<p><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>.</strong> Most uses: 1 Cor 8, Heb 5, 1 Tim 4, Rom 3, 2 Cor 3. Highest rate (2 or more uses): 1 Tim 25.1, 1 Pet 17.9, 1 Cor 11.7, Heb 10.1, 2 Cor 6.7.</p>\n<p><strong>Keyness:</strong> 1 Cor (G² 16, p &lt; 0.0001, 5.3× expected), 1 Tim (G² 13, p &lt; 0.001, 13.3× expected).</p>\n<details class=\"callout c-table\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>: every book (count, rate, expected, G²)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Book</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Acts <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span></td><td>2</td><td>1.08</td><td>4.0</td><td>1.4</td><td>below</td></tr><tr><td>Rom <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">羅馬書</span></td><td>3</td><td>4.22</td><td>1.5</td><td>1.1</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>1 Cor <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">哥林多前書</span></td><td>8</td><td>11.71</td><td>1.5</td><td>15.5</td><td>p &lt; 0.0001</td></tr><tr><td>2 Cor <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">哥林多後書</span></td><td>3</td><td>6.70</td><td>1.0</td><td>2.8</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>1 Tim <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">提摩太前書</span></td><td>4</td><td>25.14</td><td>0.3</td><td>12.7</td><td>p &lt; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td>2 Tim <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">提摩太後書</span></td><td>1</td><td>8.08</td><td>0.3</td><td>1.2</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Titus <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">提多書</span></td><td>1</td><td>15.17</td><td>0.1</td><td>2.2</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Heb <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">希伯來書</span></td><td>5</td><td>10.09</td><td>1.1</td><td>8.1</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td>1 Pet <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">彼得前書</span></td><td>3</td><td>17.87</td><td>0.4</td><td>7.6</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></details>\n<p><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>.</strong> Most uses: Acts 3, 1 Cor 1. Highest rate (2 or more uses): Acts 1.6.</p>\n<p><strong>Keyness:</strong> no book stands out at p &lt; 0.001.</p>\n<details class=\"callout c-table\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>: every book (count, rate, expected, G²)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Book</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Acts <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span></td><td>3</td><td>1.63</td><td>0.5</td><td>7.9</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td>1 Cor <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">哥林多前書</span></td><td>1</td><td>1.46</td><td>0.2</td><td>1.8</td><td>not significant</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></details>\n<p><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>.</strong> Most uses: 2 Chr 3, Dan 2, Eccl 1. Highest rate (2 or more uses): Dan 2.5, 2 Chr 1.5.</p>\n<p><strong>Keyness:</strong> no book stands out at p &lt; 0.001.</p>\n<details class=\"callout c-table\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>: every book (count, rate, expected, G²)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Book</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2 Chr <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">歷代志下</span></td><td>3</td><td>1.52</td><td>0.3</td><td>10.4</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td>Eccl <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">傳道書</span></td><td>1</td><td>2.36</td><td>0.1</td><td>3.9</td><td>p &lt; 0.05</td></tr><tr><td>Dan <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">但以理書</span></td><td>2</td><td>2.48</td><td>0.1</td><td>8.4</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></details>\n<p><em>G² (log-likelihood) compares the count in a book with what the book's size predicts; G² ≥ 10.83 means p &lt; 0.001, a chance below 1 in 1,000 that the excess is luck.</em></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-by-section-按分段\">3. By section <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">按分段</span></h3>\n<p><img class=\"emb\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"charts/S20 conscience - sections.svg\" src=\"pages/f6e83f8751.svg\"></p>\n<p><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span></strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gospels <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">福音書</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>14.1</td><td>38.0</td><td>significantly below</td></tr><tr><td>Acts <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span></td><td>2</td><td>1.08</td><td>4.0</td><td>1.4</td><td>below</td></tr><tr><td>Paul's letters <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信</span></td><td>20</td><td>6.17</td><td>7.0</td><td>25.1</td><td>p &lt; 0.0001</td></tr><tr><td>Hebrews and the General letters <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">希伯來書與普通書信</span></td><td>8</td><td>6.38</td><td>2.7</td><td>7.8</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td>Revelation <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">啟示錄</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>2.1</td><td>4.4</td><td>below</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span></strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gospels <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">福音書</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>1.9</td><td>5.1</td><td>below</td></tr><tr><td>Acts <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span></td><td>3</td><td>1.63</td><td>0.5</td><td>7.9</td><td>p &lt; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td>Paul's letters <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信</span></td><td>1</td><td>0.31</td><td>0.9</td><td>0.0</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Hebrews and the General letters <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">希伯來書與普通書信</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>0.4</td><td>0.8</td><td>below</td></tr><tr><td>Revelation <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">啟示錄</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>0.3</td><td>0.6</td><td>below</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span></strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Count</th><th>Per 10,000</th><th>Expected</th><th>G²</th><th>p</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Law <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">律法書</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>1.6</td><td>3.7</td><td>below</td></tr><tr><td>History <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">歷史書</span></td><td>3</td><td>0.19</td><td>2.2</td><td>0.5</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Wisdom and Poetry <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">詩歌智慧書</span></td><td>1</td><td>0.20</td><td>0.7</td><td>0.1</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Major Prophets <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">大先知書</span></td><td>2</td><td>0.23</td><td>1.2</td><td>0.5</td><td>not significant</td></tr><tr><td>Minor Prophets <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">小先知書</span></td><td>0</td><td>0.00</td><td>0.3</td><td>0.6</td><td>below</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"4-by-grammatical-form-按詞形\">4. By grammatical form <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">按詞形</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span> — <em>part of speech:</em> noun 30 · <em>case:</em> accusative 16, genitive 7, dative 4, nominative 3 · <em>number:</em> singular 29, plural 1</li>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span> — <em>tense:</em> perfect 2 · <em>voice:</em> active 2 · <em>mood:</em> participle 1, indicative 1</li>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span> — <em>tense:</em> second aorist 2 · <em>voice:</em> active 2 · <em>mood:</em> participle 2</li>\n<li><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span> — <em>part of speech:</em> noun 6 · <em>number:</em> singular 6 · <em>state:</em> absolute 6 · <em>pronoun suffix:</em> none 5, your 1</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"5-by-translation-按譯本\">5. By translation <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">按譯本</span></h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lemma</th><th>KJV (its own tags)</th><th>ASV (machine-tagged)</th><th><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> (alignment; full list in section 4)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span></td><td>conscience 26, sake 4, consciences 1</td><td>conscience 27, consciences 1, consciousness 1, conscience toward 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心 26, 天良 2, 心 1, 是非之心</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span></td><td>–</td><td>–</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道 1, 覺得</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></td><td>considered 1</td><td>considered 1, aware 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">想了一想 1, 知道</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></td><td>knowledge 4, thought 1, science 1</td><td>knowledge 4, science 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聰明</span> 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>The KJV counts are its own Strong's tags. The ASV's tags were added by machine and sometimes sit on the wrong word, so its counts are a guide only; \"–\" = no tag found. Small words that carry a tag (and, of, the, for, let …) are left out of both lists.</em></p>\n<h3 id=\"6-first-and-last-use-rank-hapax-首次與末次排名罕用\">6. First and last use; rank; hapax <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">首次與末次、排名、罕用</span></h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lemma</th><th>First</th><th>Last</th><th>Rank among all lemmas</th><th>Once only?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span></td><td>456 of 5,399 (NT)</td><td>no</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span></td><td>2652 of 5,399 (NT)</td><td>no</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.12.12\">Acts 12:12</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.14.6\">Acts 14:6</span></td><td>2652 of 5,399 (NT)</td><td>no</td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span></td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.17\">Dan 1:17</span></td><td>2987 of 8,563 (OT)</td><td>no</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"7-spread-分佈\">7. Spread <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">分佈</span></h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lemma / family</th><th>Books with it</th><th>DP (0 = even, 1 = one corner)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span></td><td>9 of 27</td><td>0.727</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> family</strong></td><td>9 of 27</td><td><strong>0.727</strong></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span></td><td>2 of 27</td><td>0.817</td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></td><td>1 of 27</td><td>0.866</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span> family</strong></td><td>2 of 27</td><td><strong>0.817</strong></td></tr><tr><td><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></td><td>3 of 39</td><td>0.925</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> family</strong></td><td>3 of 39</td><td><strong>0.925</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>DP (Gries' deviation of proportions): how far the word's spread over the books is from what the book sizes predict.</em></p>\n<h3 id=\"8-significance-意義\">8. Significance <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">意義</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Statistical (log-likelihood G², chi-square with 1 df):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>:</strong> sections over-represented: Paul's letters <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信</span> (G² 25, p &lt; 0.0001); books: 1 Cor (G² 16), 1 Tim (G² 13).</li>\n<li><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>:</strong> sections over-represented: none at p &lt; 0.001; books: none at p &lt; 0.001.</li>\n<li><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>:</strong> sections over-represented: none at p &lt; 0.001; books: none at p &lt; 0.001.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>In context (a judgment — the rubric of the template: F first mention · P programmatic or climactic · C covenant formula or God describing himself · Q quoted in the NT or quoting the OT · A carries the argument):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Passage</th><th>F</th><th>P</th><th>C</th><th>Q</th><th>A</th><th>Rating</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span></td><td>F</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>the first time the OT puts a clear conscience into words: \"in the integrity of my heart and the innocency of my hands have I done this\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>, ASV) (LXX <em><span lang=\"grc\">εν καθαρά καρδία</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>, ABP))</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>the witness who 'knew': <em><span lang=\"grc\">και ούτος μάρτυς η εώρακεν η συνοίδεν</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span>, ABP) — <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"that David's heart smote him\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>, ASV) — BDB's 'conscience' sense of <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"And David's heart smote him after that he had numbered the people\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>, ASV) — and he confesses, \"I have sinned greatly in that which I have done\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"My heart shall not reproach me so long as I live\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>, ASV); LXX <em><span lang=\"grc\">ου γαρ σύνοιδα εμαυτώ άτοπα πράξας</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>, ABP), the words of <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span></td><td>F</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>the only <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> of the Greek OT (LXX used here), for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> 'thought'</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span></td><td></td><td></td><td>C</td><td>Q</td><td></td><td>★★</td><td>\"I will put my law in their inward parts, and in their heart will I write it; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span>, ASV) — quoted in <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.8.10\">Heb 8:10</span> and 10:16 (S21)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Ezek.36.25\">Ezek 36:25</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"And I will sprinkle clean water upon you, and ye shall be clean\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Ezek.36.25\">Ezek 36:25</span>, ASV) — with the new heart (36:26), the picture of <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span></td><td>F</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>first <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>: \"Brethren, I have lived before God in all good conscience until this day\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"Herein I also exercise myself to have a conscience void of offence toward God and men always\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★★</td><td>\"in that they show the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience bearing witness therewith\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>, ASV) — the inner witness of every person (Bible truths 90)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"my conscience bearing witness with me in the Holy Spirit\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>, ASV) (S19)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.13.5\">Rom 13:5</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★</td><td>\"but also for conscience' sake\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.13.5\">Rom 13:5</span>, ASV) — obedience from conscience, not only from fear</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★★</td><td>\"For I know nothing against myself; yet am I not hereby justified: but he that judgeth me is the Lord\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">1 Cor 8:12</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★</td><td>\"and wounding their conscience when it is weak, ye sin against Christ\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">1 Cor 8:12</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.29\">1 Cor 10:29</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★</td><td>\"conscience, I say, not thine own, but the other's\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.29\">1 Cor 10:29</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"commending ourselves to every man's conscience in the sight of God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span>, ASV) — preaching that speaks to the conscience (S23)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"But the end of the charge is love out of a pure heart and a good conscience and faith unfeigned\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"which some having thrust from them made shipwreck concerning the faith\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"branded in their own conscience as with a hot iron\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"but both their mind and their conscience are defiled\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★★</td><td>\"gifts and sacrifices that cannot, as touching the conscience, make the worshipper perfect\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★★</td><td>the climax: \"cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★</td><td>\"would have had no more consciousness of sins\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.16\">Heb 10:16</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Q</td><td></td><td>★</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span> again: \"I will put my laws on their heart, And upon their mind also will I write them\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.16\">Heb 10:16</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td>A</td><td>★★</td><td>\"having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"we are persuaded that we have a good conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">1 Pet 3:16</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>\"having a good conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">1 Pet 3:16</span>, ASV) — before those who revile</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span></td><td>F</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>last <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>: baptism, \"the interrogation of a good conscience toward God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>, ASV)</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span></td><td></td><td>P</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>★</td><td>without the word: \"because if our heart condemn us, God is greater than our heart, and knoweth all things\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span>, ASV)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>Data behind \"A\" — where the words are densest (ten-verse stretches with three or more uses):</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.25-29\">1 Cor 10:25–29</span> (5), <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7-12\">1 Cor 8:7–12</span> (3).</li>\n<li>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>: no dense stretch.</li>\n<li>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10-12\">2 Chr 1:10–12</span> (3).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"4-和合本-renderings-和合本的譯法-every-rendering-every-verse\">4. <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> renderings <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本的譯法</span> (every rendering, every verse) <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><em>From the word-by-word alignments (OT: OpenHebrewBible CUV-to-BHS; NT: OpenGNT CUVtc). Pronouns and particles at the edges are set aside for grouping (<span lang=\"zh-Hant\">他的慈愛</span> is listed under <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">慈愛</span>, and the raw forms are kept). A use the alignment does not tie to a Chinese word is listed as \"not tied\".</em></p>\n<h4 id=\"συνείδησις-syneídēsis-g4893--30-uses-4-renderings\"><big><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span></big> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span> — 30 uses, 4 renderings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span></th><th>Count</th><th>Where (by section)</th><th>Forms in the text</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span></strong></td><td>26</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信 18, 希伯來書與普通書信 6, 使徒行傳</span> 2</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心 25, 良心說</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">天良</span></strong></td><td>2</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信 1, 希伯來書與普通書信</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">天良 1, 天良的</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">希伯來書與普通書信</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span> 1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"callout c-list\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Every verse, by rendering (G4893)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span></strong> (26): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">24:16</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.13.5\">13:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.10\">8:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">8:12</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.25\">10:25</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.27\">10:27</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.28\">10:28</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.29\">10:29</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.29\">10:29</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.1.12\">2 Cor 1:12</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">4:2</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.5.11\">5:11</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1:19</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">3:9</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">4:2</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">10:2</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">13:18</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">3:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">3:21</span><br><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">天良</span></strong> (2): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span><br><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span><br><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span></p></div></details>\n<h4 id=\"σύνοιδα-g6083--2-uses-2-renderings\"><big><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span></big> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span> — 2 uses, 2 renderings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span></th><th>Count</th><th>Where (by section)</th><th>Forms in the text</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">覺得</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">保羅書信</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">覺得</span> 1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"callout c-list\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Every verse, by rendering (G6083)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span><br><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">覺得</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span></p></div></details>\n<h4 id=\"συνείδω-syneídō-g4894--2-uses-2-renderings\"><big><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span></big> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span> — 2 uses, 2 renderings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span></th><th>Count</th><th>Where (by section)</th><th>Forms in the text</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">想了一想</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">想了一想</span> 1</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道</span></strong></td><td>1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使徒行傳</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道了</span> 1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"callout c-list\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Every verse, by rendering (G4894)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">想了一想</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.12.12\">Acts 12:12</span><br><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">知道</span></strong> (1): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.14.6\">Acts 14:6</span></p></div></details>\n<h4 id=\"מדע-maddâʻ-h4093--6-uses-1-renderings\"><big><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span></big> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span> — 6 uses, 1 renderings</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span></th><th>Count</th><th>Where (by section)</th><th>Forms in the text</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聰明</span></strong></td><td>4</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">歷史書 3, 大先知書</span> 1</td><td><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聰明</span> 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"callout c-list\"><summary class=\"ctitle\">Every verse, by rendering (H4093)</summary><div class=\"cbody\"><p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聰明</span></strong> (4): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">1:11</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.12\">1:12</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.17\">Dan 1:17</span><br><strong>Not tied to a Chinese word by the alignment</strong> (2): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.4\">Dan 1:4</span></p></div></details>\n<p><strong>What the variety shows:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>One Greek word, three Chinese ones: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> (26), <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">天良</span> (2: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「連心地和天良也都污穢了」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）; 「並我們心中天良的虧欠已經灑去」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>) and <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span> 'the heart of right and wrong' (1: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>) — all three are old Chinese moral words (section 9) — and once <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span> with the note <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">〔原文作良心〕</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>).</li>\n<li><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">無虧</span> 'without loss' is the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span>'s word for a good conscience: 'good' (<span lang=\"grc\">ἀγαθή</span>) is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「無虧的良心」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span> (also <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">1 Pet 3:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">21</span>), <span lang=\"grc\">ἀπρόσκοπος</span> is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「常存無虧的良心」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>, and 'good' (<span lang=\"grc\">καλή</span>) in <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span> is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「因我們自覺良心無虧，願意凡事按正道而行」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>. 'Pure' is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">清潔: 「要存清潔的良心」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">1 Tim 3:9</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>. The Heb 9 sermon draft takes its title from this phrase: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">無虧的良心</span>. <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span> adds words to make the sense plain: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「我在神面前行事為人都是憑着良心」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>.</li>\n<li>The accusing heart is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span> + <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">責</span> in both Testaments: 'David's heart smote him' is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心中自責</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>); <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「在世的日子，我心必不責備我」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）; 「我們的心若責備我們，神比我們的心大」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>; and \"Happy is he that judgeth not himself\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.14.22\">Rom 14:22</span>, ASV) is <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「人在自己以為可行的事上能不自責，就有福了」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.14.22\">Rom 14:22</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>.</li>\n<li>Where the sense is 'awareness' the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> turns it into an event: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「良心既被潔淨，就不再覺得有罪了」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span> ('consciousness of sins' = <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">覺得有罪</span>), and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span> <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">「倘若人為叫良心對得住神」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span>. The two <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> where the original has another word (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eph.4.19\">Eph 4:19</span> 'past feeling'; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.25.31\">1 Sam 25:31</span> 'offence of heart') are in section 1; with them the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> text has <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> in 28 verses.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"5-shades-of-meaning-意義層次\">5. Shades of meaning <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">意義層次</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><em>UBS Dictionary of Biblical Hebrew (SDBH 0.9.2) and UBS Greek NT Dictionary 1.1: each sense with its domain and its verses (Hebrew verse numbers mapped to the English ones).</em></p>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span></strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Domain</th><th>Definition</th><th>Verses</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>to know, to be conscious of, to be aware of</td><td>Know / Know</td><td>to be aware of information about something</td><td>2</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span></td></tr><tr><td>moral sensitivity, conscience</td><td>Psychological Faculties</td><td>(contrast <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> ‘knowledge about something,’ LN 28.4) the psychological faculty which can distinguish between right and wrong</td><td>27</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span></td></tr><tr><td>to refuse to listen to one’s conscience, to be completely insensitive to</td><td>Learn / Be Willing To Learn</td><td>(an idiom, literally: to be seared in the conscience, or: to be seared as to one’s conscience) to be unwilling to learn from one’s conscience</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span>: no UBS entry<br><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Domain</th><th>Definition</th><th>Verses</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>to know, to be conscious of, to be aware of</td><td>Know / Know</td><td>to be aware of information about something</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span></td></tr><tr><td>to know something together with someone else</td><td>Know / Know</td><td>to share information or knowledge with</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.2\">Acts 5:2</span></td></tr><tr><td>to learn about, to find out about</td><td>Learn / Learn</td><td>to acquire information, with focus upon the event of perception</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.14.6\">Acts 14:6</span></td></tr><tr><td>to understand clearly, to realize fully, to become fully aware of</td><td>Understand / Come To Understand</td><td>to come to understand clearly on the basis of perceived information</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.12.12\">Acts 12:12</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span></strong></p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Domain</th><th>Definition</th><th>Verses</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>knowledge, learning</td><td>Wise</td><td>literally: knowing; hence: = a collection of information stored and processed in someone's mind that gives that person the ability to analyse, discern, make …</td><td>5</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">2 Chr 1:11</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.12\">2 Chr 1:12</span></td></tr><tr><td>thought</td><td>Think</td><td>literally: knowing; hence: = process by which humans are exercising their minds about certain matters</td><td>1</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"6-the-lxx-bridge-七十士譯本的橋樑\">6. The LXX bridge <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">七十士譯本的橋樑</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><em>Verse by verse: each Hebrew verse beside its Septuagint verse. <strong>Matched</strong> = verses where the Hebrew and the Greek word are paired one to one, the strongest pair first, so a Greek word already explained by another Hebrew word in the verse is not counted again: the probable rendering, to read in the verses. <strong>Together</strong> = verses where both merely stand. <strong>× chance</strong> = together ÷ what the two verse counts predict. A row with Together but Matched 0 is a companion in the verse, not a rendering.</em></p>\n<p><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> <em>maddâʻ</em> <span class=\"off\">H4093</span> → Greek</strong> (of 6 verses with a Septuagint verse)</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Greek in the LXX</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Matched</th><th>Together</th><th>× chance</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σύνεσις</span> <em>sýnesis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4907</span></td><td>understanding</td><td>4</td><td>4</td><td>215.3</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">2 Chr 1:11</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.12\">2 Chr 1:12</span></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">φρόνησις</span> <em>phrónēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G5428</span></td><td>understanding</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>221.4</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.4\">Dan 1:4</span></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">σοφία</span> <em>sophía</em> <span class=\"off\">G4678</span></td><td>wisdom</td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>134.5</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">2 Chr 1:11</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.12\">2 Chr 1:12</span></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">πλοῦτος</span> <em>ploûtos</em> <span class=\"off\">G4149</span></td><td>riches</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>106.2</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">2 Chr 1:11</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.12\">2 Chr 1:12</span></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">συνίημι</span> <em>syníēmi</em> <span class=\"off\">G4920</span></td><td>to understand</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>72.4</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.4\">Dan 1:4</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Dan.1.17\">Dan 1:17</span></td></tr><tr><td><span lang=\"grc\">κρίνω</span> <em>krínō</em> <span class=\"off\">G2919</span></td><td>to judge</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>44.8</td><td><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.10\">2 Chr 1:10</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Chr.1.11\">2 Chr 1:11</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> <em>syneídēsis</em> <span class=\"off\">G4893</span> ← the Hebrew behind it in the LXX</strong> (of 1 verses)</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hebrew</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Matched</th><th>Together</th><th>× chance</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> <span class=\"off\">G6083</span>:</strong> not in the LXX notes (0 verses with a Hebrew verse beside it), so there is no bridge to read.</p>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> <em>syneídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G4894</span> ← the Hebrew behind it in the LXX</strong> (of 2 verses)</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hebrew</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Matched</th><th>Together</th><th>× chance</th><th>For example</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>OT verses with these Hebrew words that the NT quotes</strong> (chart <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">舊約在新約</span> The Old Testament in the New, verse by verse: a list, or OpenBible where the tagged words have no list address, names the link, the NT words are tagged as an OT quotation (Levinsohn), and the two verses share words): none listed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Greek OT has the noun once (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span> 'thought') and the verb twice: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span> (for <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יָדַע</span>, the witness who 'knew') and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span> (for 'my heart shall not reproach me'). The LXX used here tags both verbs G4894 (the Apostolic Bible Polyglot's numbers); OpenGNT gives the perfect <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span> its own number, G6083. Abbott-Smith adds Wis 17:11 and Sir 42:18 (one manuscript); the LXX used here has no Apocrypha. The LXX used here is the Sixtine of 1587 via Bos 1709, not Rahlfs-Hanhart.</li>\n<li>Where the Hebrew says the heart smote David, the LXX keeps the heart: <em><span lang=\"grc\">και επάταξε καρδία Δαυίδ αυτόν</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>, ABP) (also <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>). Abimelech's 'integrity of heart' becomes a 'pure heart', <em><span lang=\"grc\">εν καθαρά καρδία</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5\">Gen 20:5</span>, ABP) — the phrase Paul sets beside the good conscience: <em><span lang=\"grc\">ἐκ καθαρᾶς καρδίας καὶ συνειδήσεως ἀγαθῆς</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, OpenGNT).</li>\n<li>The law on the heart: <em><span lang=\"grc\">δώσω νόμους μου εις την διάνοιαν αυτών και επί καρδίας αυτών γράψω αυτούς</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span>, ABP) passes into <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.8.10\">Heb 8:10</span> and 10:16 (S21). Paul's Gentiles show <em><span lang=\"grc\">τὸ ἔργον τοῦ νόμου γραπτὸν ἐν ταῖς καρδίαις αὐτῶν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>, OpenGNT), 'written in their hearts', with the conscience as co-witness; whether Paul is echoing Jeremiah there, and who these Gentiles are, is read in more than one way (one view among several).</li>\n<li>Cleansing: the red heifer's 'water for impurity' is <em><span lang=\"grc\">ύδωρ ραντισμού</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Num.19.9\">Num 19:9</span>, ABP) ('water of sprinkling'), which <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.13\">Heb 9:13</span> recalls, <em><span lang=\"grc\">σποδὸς δαμάλεως ῥαντίζουσα</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.13\">Heb 9:13</span>, OpenGNT); Ezekiel's promise, <em><span lang=\"grc\">και ρανώ εφ΄ υμάς καθαρόν ύδωρ</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Ezek.36.25\">Ezek 36:25</span>, ABP), stands beside the new heart (36:26). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span> has both pictures in one line: <em><span lang=\"grc\">ῥεραντισμένοι τὰς καρδίας ἀπὸ συνειδήσεως πονηρᾶς καὶ λελουσμένοι τὸ σῶμα ὕδατι καθαρῷ</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>, OpenGNT).</li>\n<li>A verse close to the idea, without the word: \"The spirit of man is the lamp of Jehovah, Searching all his innermost parts\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Prov.20.27\">Prov 20:27</span>, ASV) — the Hebrew is <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">נִשְׁמַ֣ת אָדָ֑ם</span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Prov.20.27\">Prov 20:27</span>, BHSA) ('the breath of man', not <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">רוּחַ</span>), the LXX <em><span lang=\"grc\">φως κυρίου πνοή ανθρώπων</span></em> (LXX <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Prov.20.27\">Prov 20:27</span>, ABP).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"7-companions-and-cross-references-同伴字與互參\">7. Companions and cross-references <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">同伴字與互參</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p><em>Words that stand with it far more often than chance. Same verse, and within two verses either side (same book). Ranked by G²; PMI = log₂(observed ÷ expected): 1 = twice as often as chance, 3 = eight times.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>, same verse:</strong> <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρός</span> clean (5; PMI 5.9, G² 33), <span lang=\"grc\">λατρεύω</span> to minister (4; PMI 5.7, G² 25), <span lang=\"grc\">ἐσθίω</span> to eat (5; PMI 4.64, G² 24), <span lang=\"grc\">εἰδωλόθυτον</span> sacrificed to idols (3; PMI 6.36, G² 22), <span lang=\"grc\">ἀγαθός</span> good-doer (5; PMI 3.91, G² 19), <span lang=\"grc\">προσφέρω</span> to bring to (3; PMI 4.19, G² 12), <span lang=\"grc\">μηδείς</span> nothing (3; PMI 3.24, G² 8), <span lang=\"grc\">πίστις</span> faith/trust (4; PMI 2.27, G² 7), <span lang=\"grc\">χάρις</span> grace (3; PMI 2.48, G² 6), <span lang=\"grc\">καρδία</span> heart (3; PMI 2.46, G² 6).</p>\n<p><strong>Greek conscience <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span>, within two verses:</strong> <span lang=\"grc\">εἰδωλόθυτον</span> sacrificed to idols (6; PMI 5.22, G² 34), <span lang=\"grc\">ἀγαθός</span> good-doer (11; PMI 2.93, G² 30), <span lang=\"grc\">ἄπιστος</span> unbelieving (6; PMI 4.34, G² 26), <span lang=\"grc\">βρῶμα</span> food (5; PMI 4.19, G² 21), <span lang=\"grc\">ἐσθίω</span> to eat (7; PMI 3.18, G² 20), <span lang=\"grc\">παρατίθημι</span> to set before (5; PMI 3.99, G² 19), <span lang=\"grc\">λατρεύω</span> to minister (5; PMI 3.7, G² 17), <span lang=\"grc\">μηνύω</span> to disclose (3; PMI 5.36, G² 17), <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρός</span> clean (5; PMI 3.65, G² 17), <span lang=\"grc\">ἀνακρίνω</span> to investigate (4; PMI 4.21, G² 17).</p>\n<p><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>, same verse:</strong> .</p>\n<p><strong>Greek to know with, be aware <span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα, συνεῖδον</span>, within two verses:</strong> .</p>\n<p><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>, same verse:</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">חׇכְמָה</span> wisdom (5; PMI 7.1, G² 46), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מֶלֶךְ</span> king (3; PMI 2.59, G² 7).</p>\n<p><strong>Hebrew knowledge, thought <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מַדָּע</span>, within two verses:</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">נֶכֶס</span> riches (3; PMI 9.25, G² 35), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">חׇכְמָה</span> wisdom (5; PMI 5.08, G² 32), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">עֹשֶׁר</span> riches (3; PMI 6.13, G² 21), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">מֶלֶךְ</span> king (6; PMI 2.19, G² 18), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יוֹם</span> day (6; PMI 1.73, G² 14), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">פָּנִים</span> face (6; PMI 1.69, G² 14), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יַיִן</span> wine (3; PMI 4.3, G² 14), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">שָׂנֵא</span> hate (3; PMI 4.13, G² 13), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">שְׁלֹמֹה</span> Solomon (3; PMI 4.04, G² 13), <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">רַב</span> much (4; PMI 3.02, G² 13).</p>\n<p><strong>Pairs: do the two words stand together?</strong> (verses with both; chance = what the two verse counts predict; G² for the 2 × 2 table of verses)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">ἀγαθός</span>:</strong> 5 verses with both, chance alone 0.3 → more than chance, G² 18.8 (p &lt; 0.0001). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.23.1\">Acts 23:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1:19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">1 Pet 3:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">3:21</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρός</span>:</strong> 5 verses with both, chance alone 0.1 → more than chance, G² 33.1 (p &lt; 0.0001). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">3:9</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">πίστις</span>:</strong> 4 verses with both, chance alone 0.8 → more than chance, G² 6.7 (p &lt; 0.01). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1:19</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">3:9</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">καρδία</span>:</strong> 3 verses with both, chance alone 0.5 → more than chance, G² 5.6 (p &lt; 0.05). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">λατρεύω</span>:</strong> 4 verses with both, chance alone 0.1 → more than chance, G² 25.1 (p &lt; 0.0001). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">9:14</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">10:2</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">συμμαρτυρέω</span>:</strong> 2 verses with both, chance alone 0.0 → more than chance, G² 18.8 (p &lt; 0.0001). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">9:1</span></li>\n<li><strong><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">ἀσθενής</span>:</strong> 2 verses with both, chance alone 0.1 → more than chance, G² 9.0 (p &lt; 0.01). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.10\">8:10</span></li>\n<li><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> keeps company with <span lang=\"grc\">πίστις</span> 'faith' (4 verses (chance alone 0.8): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">3:9</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span> — \"holding faith and a good conscience; which some having thrust from them made shipwreck concerning the faith\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span>, ASV)), with <span lang=\"grc\">καρδία</span> 'heart' (3 verses (chance alone 0.5): <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>) and with <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρός</span> 'pure' (5 verses (chance alone 0.1); 'a pure conscience' itself twice, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">1 Tim 3:9</span> and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>; the other three verses have 'pure' nearby).</li>\n<li>With the cleansing words of Hebrews: <span lang=\"grc\">καθαρίζω</span> 'cleanse' (2 verses (chance alone 0.1): 9:14; 10:2) and <span lang=\"grc\">λατρεύω</span> 'serve, worship' (4 verses (chance alone 0.1)); with <span lang=\"grc\">αἷμα</span> 'blood' once, 9:14 — one verse that holds blood, the Spirit, the conscience, dead works and worship together.</li>\n<li>With the other studies of this set: the Holy Spirit (S19: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span> 'through the eternal Spirit'), covenant (S21: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span> → <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.8.10\">Heb 8:10</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.16\">10:16</span>), church (S22: the weak brother's conscience, \"the brother for whose sake Christ died\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.11\">1 Cor 8:11</span>, ASV)), word (S23: \"nor handling the word of God deceitfully … commending ourselves to every man's conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span>, ASV)).</li>\n<li>Verse cross-references: \"Old in New\" is used in section 6.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"8-in-the-new-testament-新約的用法\">8. In the New Testament <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">新約的用法</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<p>By section (from 3.3): Gospels 0, Acts 5, Paul's letters 21, Hebrews and the General letters 8, Revelation 0.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The family of <span lang=\"grc\">εἴδω</span> <em>eídō</em> <span class=\"off\">G1492</span> (Strong): <span lang=\"grc\">ἀπείδω</span> 0×, <span lang=\"grc\">εἶδος</span> 5×, <span lang=\"grc\">ἐπεῖδον</span> 2×, <span lang=\"grc\">ἰδέα</span> 1×, <span lang=\"grc\">ἴσος</span> 8×, <span lang=\"grc\">ἱστορέω</span> 1×, <span lang=\"grc\">προείδω</span> 0×, <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span> 2×, <span lang=\"grc\">ὑπερείδω</span> 1×</li>\n<li>By book: Paul's letters 20 (1 Corinthians 8, 1 Timothy 4, Romans 3, 2 Corinthians 3, 2 Timothy 1, Titus 1), Hebrews 5, 1 Peter 3, Acts 2; none in the Gospels, James, John's letters or Revelation. Abbott-Smith and the UBS dictionary both set <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span> and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span> apart as 'consciousness, awareness' (section 5): <em><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησιν ἁμαρτιῶν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">Heb 10:2</span>, OpenGNT) 'consciousness of sins', <em><span lang=\"grc\">διὰ συνείδησιν Θεοῦ</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>, OpenGNT) ('because of awareness of God'; ASV \"for conscience toward God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>, ASV)).</li>\n<li>1 Corinthians 8 and 10 (8 of the 30): believers long used to idols have a weak conscience; eating defiles it (8:7); the knowing brother's example will 'build it up' to eat — <em><span lang=\"grc\">οἰκοδομηθήσεται</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.10\">1 Cor 8:10</span>, OpenGNT), the word for edifying (ASV 'emboldened'; many read an irony here); and striking it is sin against Christ: <em><span lang=\"grc\">τύπτοντες αὐτῶν τὴν συνείδησιν ἀσθενοῦσαν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">1 Cor 8:12</span>, OpenGNT), \"and wounding their conscience when it is weak, ye sin against Christ\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">1 Cor 8:12</span>, ASV). In chapter 10 the rule is freedom with love: \"Whatsoever is sold in the shambles, eat, asking no question for conscience' sake\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.25\">1 Cor 10:25</span>, ASV), but when someone points it out, \"conscience, I say, not thine own, but the other's\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.29\">1 Cor 10:29</span>, ASV). Rom 14 teaches the same without the word: \"and whatsoever is not of faith is sin\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.14.23\">Rom 14:23</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li>The pastoral letters (6 of the 30): love comes \"out of a pure heart and a good conscience and faith unfeigned\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, ASV); some thrust the good conscience away and \"made shipwreck concerning the faith\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span>, ASV); deacons hold \"the mystery of the faith in a pure conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">1 Tim 3:9</span>, ASV); false teachers are branded in their own conscience (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>); Paul serves God \"from my forefathers in a pure conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Tim.1.3\">2 Tim 1:3</span>, ASV); to the defiled \"both their mind and their conscience are defiled\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>, ASV). Faith and conscience stand and fall together.</li>\n<li>The text differs (the Greek behind the KJV, the Textus Receptus, against OpenGNT ≈ NA28): (1) <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.8.9\">John 8:9</span> — the KJV adds \"being convicted by their own conscience\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.8.9\">John 8:9</span>, KJV); OpenGNT's verse has no such words (ASV \"And they, when they heard it, went out one by one\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.8.9\">John 8:9</span>, ASV)), and Abbott-Smith marks the phrase '(Rec.)', the Received Text; the passage <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.7.53-53,John.8.1-11\">John 7:53–8:11</span> itself is absent from the oldest Greek manuscripts. (2) <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span> — the KJV reads \"for some with conscience of the idol unto this hour eat it\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, KJV), OpenGNT <em><span lang=\"grc\">τῇ συνηθείᾳ ἕως ἄρτι τοῦ εἰδώλου</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, OpenGNT), 'by custom', as the ASV \"being used until now to the idol\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.7\">1 Cor 8:7</span>, ASV): the KJV has 'conscience' twice in that verse, OpenGNT once. (3) <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.28\">1 Cor 10:28</span> — the KJV repeats \"for the earth is the Lord’s, and the fulness thereof\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.28\">1 Cor 10:28</span>, KJV) (from 10:26), not in OpenGNT. (4) <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span> — OpenGNT <em><span lang=\"grc\">καθαριεῖ τὴν συνείδησιν ἡμῶν</span></em> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, OpenGNT), 'our conscience'; the KJV and the ASV say 'your'. (5) <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span> — OpenGNT <span lang=\"grc\">ὑμᾶς</span> 'you', the KJV \"doth also now save us\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>, KJV). The editions (SBLGNT apparatus: Westcott–Hort, Tregelles, NA28, Robinson–Pierpont; Scrivener's TR of 1894; compared 1 Nov 2026): in all five the KJV's reading is that of Robinson–Pierpont's Byzantine text and of the TR (in the SBLGNT apparatus the whole of <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.7.53-53,John.8.1-11\">John 7:53–8:11</span> is Robinson–Pierpont's, with the phrase in 8:9); Westcott–Hort, Tregelles and NA28 read with OpenGNT in the other four, except that Tregelles reads 'your' in <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, as the ASV.</li>\n<li><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>: <span lang=\"grc\">ἐπερώτημα</span> stands only here in the NT. Abbott-Smith: '1. a question, an inquiry (Hdt., Thuc.). 2. a demand: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">I Pe 3:21</span>'; the ASV says 'the interrogation', the KJV 'the answer', the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本 「只求在神面前有無虧的良心」（</span><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">，和合本）</span> ('only seeking a good conscience before God'). Whether baptism is the believer's appeal to God for a good conscience, or the pledge that a good conscience makes to God, is read both ways (one view among several).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"9-culture-and-background-文化背景\">9. Culture and background <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">文化背景</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Greek moral language: Abbott-Smith dates the ethical sense to the 'Stoics and late writers', and LSJ quotes <span lang=\"grc\">βροτοῖς ἅπασιν ἡ σ. θεός</span> (section 2). Paul could speak to Greeks with a word they knew — \"commending ourselves to every man's conscience in the sight of God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span>, ASV) — and then set it before God.</li>\n<li>Chinese: <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> and <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span> are words of Mencius (<span lang=\"zh-Hant\">孟子, 告子上</span> for <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心; 告子上</span> and <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">公孫丑上</span> for <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">是非之心</span>). For Mencius the <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> is the good heart every person is born with; the NT's <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> is a witness that knows with us, and it can be weak, defiled or branded, and is cleansed only by Christ's blood (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>). The Chinese word opens a door for the gospel, and the gospel corrects the word.</li>\n<li>The red heifer (Num 19): its ashes, kept \"for a water for impurity\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Num.19.9\">Num 19:9</span>, ASV), cleansed those defiled by touching the dead (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Num.19.9\">Num 19:9</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Num.19.11-19\">11–19</span>). <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.13\">Heb 9:13</span> recalls it, and 9:14 says 'how much more' — from the defilement of death to the conscience defiled by 'dead works'. In our day the search for a flawless red heifer for a rebuilt temple (World Watch, 2022) shows that people still look for a cleansing sacrifice; Hebrews says it was offered once for all (9:12, 26; 10:10).</li>\n<li>Luther at Worms (1521), as his words are usually reported: his conscience was 'captive to the Word of God' (Wikipedia, Diet of Worms). The principle beneath it is common ground for all the traditions: \"We must obey God rather than men\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.29\">Acts 5:29</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li>Eric Liddell, Paris 1924 (World Watch; the film Chariots of Fire, 1981): he would not run the heats of the 100 metres on a Sunday and ran the 400 metres instead — a conscience kept toward God at a cost, whatever one thinks of the Sunday question itself: \"Let each man be fully assured in his own mind\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.14.5\">Rom 14:5</span>, ASV).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"10-theology-神學\">10. Theology <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">神學</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every person has a conscience (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.14-15\">Rom 2:14–15</span>): the work of the law written on the heart, the conscience bearing witness, the thoughts accusing or excusing — so no one is left without a witness (Bible truths 90). But it is not God's voice without error: it can be weak (1 Cor 8), defiled (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>), branded (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>), and even a clear conscience does not justify (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>); the Lord is the judge, and \"God is greater than our heart\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li>Ritual cannot reach the conscience (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.1-4\">10:1–4</span>): the old sacrifices cleansed 'the flesh' (9:13) and left \"But in those sacrifices there is a remembrance made of sins year by year\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.3\">Heb 10:3</span>, ASV). Christ's blood, offered \"through the eternal Spirit\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, ASV), cleanses the conscience \"from dead works to serve the living God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>, ASV), so the believer draws near with a heart sprinkled (10:22). This is the forgiveness of sins promised in the new covenant: \"And their sins and their iniquities will I remember no more\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.17\">Heb 10:17</span>, ASV) (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.34\">Jer 31:34</span>; Bible truths 11, 37).</li>\n<li>A good conscience is kept by faith and shows itself in life: love from a good conscience (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>), faith and a good conscience held together (1:19), the wish to live honourably in all things (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span>), a gentle answer to those who revile (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.15-16\">1 Pet 3:15–16</span>), and baptism as its appeal or pledge toward God (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>; Bible truths 62).</li>\n<li>Conscience and others: freedom is limited by love for the weak brother's conscience (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.9-13\">1 Cor 8:9–13</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.23-33\">10:23–33</span>; Rom 14); authorities are obeyed \"for conscience' sake\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.13.5\">Rom 13:5</span>, ASV), and unjust suffering is borne \"for conscience toward God\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>, ASV); but where men command what God forbids, \"We must obey God rather than men\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.5.29\">Acts 5:29</span>, ASV).</li>\n<li>Where the traditions differ — how far a sincerely erring conscience binds, and what authority a church has over the conscience — the study names the difference and does not decide it (one view among several).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"12-for-practice-應用\">11. For practice <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">應用</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Teaching slide: <span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> = <span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> 'with' + <span lang=\"grc\">οἶδα</span> 'know': 'knowing with oneself', the inner witness (<span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span>). Four states — weak (1 Cor 8), defiled (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>), branded (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">1 Tim 4:2</span>), good and pure (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.3.9\">3:9</span>) — and one cure (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>).</li>\n<li>Bible class: read <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.14-15\">Rom 2:14–15</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span> and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.19-21\">1 John 3:19–21</span> — what the conscience can do and what it cannot; then <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9-14\">Heb 9:9–14</span> and 10:19–22 — what Christ does for it. In the OT: David's heart smote him (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>), and Job's did not (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>).</li>\n<li>Pastoral care: for someone who cannot forgive himself — <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span> and 10:22 (the conscience cleansed by Christ's blood, not by our feelings) and \"God is greater than our heart\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1John.3.20\">1 John 3:20</span>, ASV); for strong believers — <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.12\">1 Cor 8:12</span>: love limits liberty.</li>\n<li>Preaching: 'how much more' (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>) — if the ashes of a heifer cleansed the body, how much more the blood of Christ the conscience; and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span> as a daily aim: \"a conscience void of offence toward God and men always\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, ASV).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">連在一起</span> Connected</strong> — how they relate · why it matters · how we live it out:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bible truths <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">聖經真理</span>:</strong> <span class=\"off\">Lesson 90 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>) stands on this study, with <span class=\"off\">11 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">罪得赦免</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.17-22\">10:17–22</span>), <span class=\"off\">37 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">新約</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Jer.31.33\">Jer 31:33</span> → <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.16\">Heb 10:16</span>), <span class=\"off\">33 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">稱義</span></span> (\"yet am I not hereby justified\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>, ASV)) and <span class=\"off\">62 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">洗禮</span></span> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span>) · the conscience witnesses, Christ cleanses · bring an accusing conscience to the cross, not to self-effort.</li>\n<li><strong>Book studies <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">書卷研究</span>:</strong> <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i7a592efe93\">Hebrews</a> (<span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span> 5 times, 9:9–10:22 and 13:18) · the old worship could not reach the conscience; Christ's sacrifice does · worship with a cleansed conscience, not a guilty one.</li>\n\n<li><strong>World Watch <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">世界觀察</span>:</strong> <span class=\"off\">The red heifers</span> — the search for a flawless red heifer for a rebuilt temple · <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.13-14\">Heb 9:13–14</span>: the heifer cleansed the flesh, Christ's blood cleanses the conscience · trust the sacrifice already offered once for all.</li>\n<li><strong>World Watch <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">世界觀察</span>:</strong> <span class=\"off\">Eric Liddell, Paris 1924</span> — he would not run the 100 metres heats on a Sunday · \"a conscience void of offence toward God and men always\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Acts.24.16\">Acts 24:16</span>, ASV) · keep faith with conscience in small things too.</li>\n<li><strong>World Watch <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">世界觀察</span>:</strong> <span class=\"off\">Volkswagen 2015</span> — software that cheated the emissions tests · \"not walking in craftiness\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span>, ASV) and \"desiring to live honorably in all things\" (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">Heb 13:18</span>, ASV) · honesty when no one is testing.</li>\n<li><strong>Word studies <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">原文研究</span>:</strong> <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#ib780684f8b\">S19 Holy Spirit</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">Rom 9:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">Heb 9:14</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#ic4045911a0\">S12 perfection</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span> <span lang=\"grc\">τελειῶσαι</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i8d544e8b31\">S15 repentance</a> (dead works, 6:1; 9:14) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i73e26ca9e7\">S11 sympathize</a> (<span lang=\"grc\">ἀσθένεια</span>; the weak conscience, 1 Cor 8) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i8f24a8c218\">S9 faith</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">1 Tim 1:19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">Heb 10:22</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#ib9021d39fb\">S10 high priest</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.7-14\">Heb 9:7–14</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i697f57f936\">S7 harden</a> (the heart) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#ib30e807514\">S21 covenant</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.16\">Heb 10:16</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i16be447d20\">S22 church</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.8.11-12\">1 Cor 8:11–12</span>) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#i79bfc38b15\">S23 word</a> (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">2 Cor 4:2</span>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span lang=\"zh-Hant\">標籤詞</span> Tag words</strong> — <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">中文</span> · English · Hebrew · Greek (the shared vocabulary; counts = words in the text; a Hebrew or Greek word opens its word study, or its lexicon entry where no study exists yet):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>#t/conscience <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心</span> · conscience · <span class=\"off\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span></span> H3820 (593) · <span class=\"off\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵבָב</span></span> H3824 (252) · <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#ibc63b4f664\"><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδησις</span></a> G4893 (30) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"grc\">σύνοιδα</span></span> G6083 (2) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"grc\">συνείδω</span></span> G4894 (2)</li>\n<li>#t/heart <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">心</span> · heart · <span class=\"off\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב</span></span> H3820 (593) · <span class=\"off\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵבָב</span></span> H3824 (252) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"grc\">καρδία</span></span> G2588 (156)</li>\n<li>#t/blood <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">血</span> · blood · <span class=\"off\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">דָּם</span></span> H1818 (360) · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"grc\">αἷμα</span></span> G129 (97)</li>\n<li>#t/baptism <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">洗禮</span> · baptism · <span class=\"off\"><span lang=\"grc\">βάπτισμα</span></span> G908 (19)</li>\n<li>grammar <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">文法</span>: <span class=\"off\">construct chain <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">附屬鏈</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לֵב־ דָּוִ֖ד</span>, 1 Sam 24:5)</span> (<span class=\"off\">page 4 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>) · <span class=\"off\">suffixes on nouns <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">名詞上的代名詞詞尾</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">בְּ מַדָּֽעֲךָ֗</span>, Eccl 10:20; <span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">לְ֝בָבִ֗י</span>, Job 27:6)</span> (<span class=\"off\">page 4 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>) · <span class=\"off\">the imperfect <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">未完成式</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יֶחֱרַ֥ף</span>, Job 27:6)</span> (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>) · <span class=\"off\">a hateph vowel under a guttural <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">喉音下的</span> hateph (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">יֶחֱרַ֥ף</span>)</span> (<span class=\"off\">page 1 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>) · <span class=\"off\">Hiphil <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">使動</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"he\">וַ יַּ֥ךְ</span>, 1 Sam 24:5)</span> (<span class=\"off\">page 2 <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">圖</span></span>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"13-evaluation-評估\">12. Evaluation <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">評估</span> <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Why it matters:</strong> the conscience is where a person meets God's law inside. </li>\n<li><strong>Where it is strongest:</strong> <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.15\">Rom 2:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.9.1\">9:1</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.13.5\">13:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.4\">1 Cor 4:4</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.4.8\">8</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Cor.10.25-29\">10:25–29</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.1.12\">2 Cor 1:12</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Cor.4.2\">4:2</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.5\">1 Tim 1:5</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.1.19\">19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Tim.4.2\">4:2</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Titus.1.15\">Titus 1:15</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.9\">Heb 9:9</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.9.14\">14</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.2\">10:2</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.10.22\">22</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Heb.13.18\">13:18</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.16\">3:16</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">21</span>; in the OT, by the heart: <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Gen.20.5-6\">Gen 20:5–6</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Sam.24.5\">1 Sam 24:5</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"2Sam.24.10\">2 Sam 24:10</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>.</li>\n<li><strong>For whom:</strong> the congregation (an accusing conscience, a cleansed conscience), new believers (1 Cor 8 and Rom 14 on doubtful things), the Bible class (<span lang=\"grc\">σύν</span> + <span lang=\"grc\">οἶδα</span>; <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">良心, 天良, 是非之心</span>; the heart in the OT), the Hebrews series (9:9–10:22).</li>\n<li><strong>Limits:</strong> the data give forms, counts, translations and the differences of the Greek texts. What the conscience is (a faculty, God's voice, a judgment) is a question of theology and philosophy, and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Rom.2.14-15\">Rom 2:14–15</span> and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.3.21\">1 Pet 3:21</span> are read in more than one way; these are marked as such.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"14-sources-and-to-check-資料與待查\">13. Sources 資料 <a class=\"up\" href=\"#1-at-a-glance-%E4%B8%80%E8%A6%BD\" title=\"回到摘要 back to the summary\">↑</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Texts and tags: BHSA (ETCBC), OpenGNT 3.3, the chart <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">舊約在新約</span> The Old Testament in the New with OpenBible.info verse votes for section 6, eBible KJV 1769 and ASV 1901 with Strong's tags, OpenHebrewBible and OpenGNT <span lang=\"zh-Hant\">和合本</span> alignments, UBS SDBH and UBS Greek NT dictionaries, ISBE (1915).</li>\n<li>Editions: 和合本; KJV 1769; ASV 1901; BHSA (Hebrew); OpenGNT (Greek NT); LXX = the Apostolic Bible Polyglot (the Sixtine of 1587 as reprinted by Bos 1709, not Rahlfs–Hanhart); Textus Receptus = Scrivener 1894 where it is named.</li>\n<li>The LXX used here (the Apostolic Bible Polyglot) is the Sixtine of 1587 via Bos 1709, not Rahlfs-Hanhart; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Eccl.10.20\">Eccl 10:20</span>, <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Lev.5.1\">Lev 5:1</span> and <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span> here are that text. Abbott-Smith's Wis 17:11 and Sir 42:18 (one manuscript, Sinaiticus first hand) are not in the LXX used here, which has only the 39 books.</li>\n<li><span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"John.7.53-53,John.8.1-11\">John 7:53–8:11</span>: the KJV's phrase in 8:9 ('(Rec.)' in Abbott-Smith) is Robinson–Pierpont's and the TR's.</li>\n\n\n<li>The English renderings of the LXX lines (<span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"Job.27.6\">Job 27:6</span>; <span class=\"ilref\" tabindex=\"0\" data-q=\"1Pet.2.19\">1 Pet 2:19</span>'s Greek) are plain renderings.</li>\n</ul>\n<details class=\"pn across\" open><summary>跨燈 <i lang=\"en\">Across the lamps</i></summary><p class=\"acr\" data-b=\"1\"></p></details>"}});
